sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Durable processing and an ambiguous delivery retry
    accDescr: Input remains replayable while processing saves an immutable result and a waiting-index intent. The existing search write must succeed before the intent becomes ready and the input is acknowledged. Delivery claims ready work using a lease and token. A customer can apply an effect but lose its response. The dispatcher records an unknown outcome and durable retry time, then retries the same key and payload. A cooperating recipient deduplicates the effect. Conditional updates prevent stale attempts from changing accepted status, exhausted work remains visible for recovery.
    participant B as Event buffer
    participant P as Processing
    participant E as Enrichment
    participant S as Event state + intents
    participant I as Search index
    participant D as Delivery dispatcher
    participant C as Customer endpoint
    B->>P: Receive event, keep replay ownership
    P->>S: Lookup tenant + event ID
    S-->>P: Existing state or absent
    alt Existing ready or terminal intent
        P->>B: Acknowledge duplicate input without recreating work
    else New event or waiting-index intent
        opt No saved result
            P->>E: Enrich within deadline and concurrency limit
            E-->>P: Enriched payload
            P->>S: Atomic unique result + waiting-index intent
            S-->>P: Durable commit confirmed
        end
        Note over P,I: Pending input resumes here using the saved payload
        P->>I: Idempotent event write
        I-->>P: Write acknowledged
        Note over B,I: Index success path shown, failures retain replay ownership and defer with a budget
        P->>S: Conditionally mark waiting-index intent ready
        S-->>P: Durable ready state confirmed
        P->>B: Acknowledge input
    end
    Note over S,D: Only ready or due-retry intents may be claimed
    D->>S: Claim due intent, persist lease, token and attempt
    S-->>D: Stable delivery key + immutable payload
    D->>C: Deliver with stable key
    C->>C: Atomically record dedup key and apply effect
    C--xD: Acceptance response lost
    D->>S: Commit unknown outcome + retry time, release lease with token
    S-->>D: Durable retry confirmed
    Note over S,D: Failed state write leaves lease recoverable, no in-memory-only retry
    D->>S: Claim when due, enforce limits and remaining budget
    S-->>D: Same key and payload, new attempt token
    D->>C: Repeat delivery with same key
    C->>C: Recognize key, do not repeat effect
    C-->>D: Return prior acceptance
    D->>S: Conditionally commit endpoint-accepted, clear due work
    S-->>D: Durable outcome confirmed
    Note over S,C: Expired workers cannot regress status, overlapping requests still need recipient deduplication
    Note over B,S: Permanent failures or exhausted age/attempt budgets become durable needs-attention work
